    "description": "Hospital, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Needs scaffolding: 12 tall. Over budget: 1,536 blocks vs the infirmary's 285 (no hospital budget in the brief; under the landmark 1,800). Saved as its own structure: the infirmary's tier-6 big brother, a two-storey cloister hospital round a 5 x 5 herb courtyard: stone brick ground storey, white plaster in a dark oak frame above, one spruce roof round the ring with a cross gable over the door and a kiln chimney. 14 beds (three a side on each floor, two more upstairs at the back), dispensary, healers' room, herb store, clay room (rebuilding fallen soldiers), a staircase; courtyard pool by the decoration step. L2 brewing stands, cauldrons, candles, chained lanterns, carpets, courtyard herbs, planters, a door canopy, the red-cross banner, shutters, clay; L3 more red-cross banners, a herb garden strip, lantern posts at the gate, a log pile, barrels. Decoration step adds: water.",
